{"id":"mahabharata-3-159","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":159,"title":"एकोनषष्ट्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 159 · Kubera's counsel","summary":{"en":"Kubera teaches Yudhishthira that a king needs firmness, skill, knowledge of time and place, and courage, and warns Bhima against rashness. He promises protection and hospitality on the mountain until Arjuna's return, and the Pandavas spend the night in his halls.","kn":"ರಾಜನಿಗೆ ಧೈರ್ಯ, ದಕ್ಷತೆ, ದೇಶಕಾಲಜ್ಞಾನ, ಪರಾಕ್ರಮ ಬೇಕೆಂದು ಕುಬೇರನು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನಿಗೆ ಉಪದೇಶಿಸಿ ಭೀಮನಿಗೆ ದುಡುಕಬೇಡ ಎಂದು ಎಚ್ಚರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅರ್ಜುನನು ಮರಳುವವರೆಗೆ ಪರ್ವತದಲ್ಲಿ ರಕ್ಷಣೆ ಆತಿಥ್ಯದ ಭರವಸೆ ನೀಡುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಪಾಂಡವರು ಅವನ ಭವನಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ರಾತ್ರಿ ಕಳೆಯುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"कुबेर युधिष्ठिर को सिखाते हैं कि राजा को धैर्य, दक्षता, देश-काल का ज्ञान और पराक्रम चाहिए, और भीम को दुस्साहस से सावधान करते हैं। वे अर्जुन के लौटने तक पर्वत पर रक्षा और आतिथ्य का वचन देते हैं, और पाण्डव उनके भवनों में रात बिताते हैं।","te":"రాజుకు ధైర్యం, దక్షత, దేశకాల జ్ఞానం, పరాక్రమం అవసరమని కుబేరుడు యుధిష్ఠిరునికి ఉపదేశించి భీమునికి దుందుడుకుతనం వద్దని హెచ్చరిస్తాడు. అర్జునుడు తిరిగివచ్చే వరకు పర్వతంపై రక్షణ, ఆతిథ్యానికి హామీ ఇస్తాడు; పాండవులు ఆయన భవనాలలో రాత్రి గడుపుతారు.","ta":"மன்னனுக்கு உறுதி, திறமை, இடம் காலம் அறிவு, வீரம் தேவை என்று குபேரன் யுதிஷ்டிரருக்கு உபதேசித்துப் பீமனைத் துடுக்கு வேண்டாம் என்று எச்சரிக்கிறான். அர்ஜுனன் திரும்பும் வரை மலையில் பாதுகாப்பும் விருந்தோம்பலும் அளிப்பதாக வாக்களிக்க, பாண்டவர்கள் அவன் மாளிகைகளில் இரவைக் கழிக்கிறார்கள்.","ml":"ഭരണാധികാരിക്ക് ഉറപ്പ്, വൈദഗ്ധ്യം, കാലദേശങ്ങളെക്കുറിച്ചുള്ള അറിവ്, ധൈര്യം എന്നിവ വേണമെന്ന് കുബേരൻ യുധിഷ്ഠിരനെ പഠിപ്പിക്കുന്നു; ഭീമന്റെ അവിവേകത്തിനെതിരെ അദ്ദേഹം മുന്നറിയിപ്പ് നൽകുന്നു. അർജുനൻ മടങ്ങിവരുംവരെ പർവതത്തിൽ സംരക്ഷണവും ആതിഥ്യവും നൽകാമെന്ന് വാഗ്ദാനം ചെയ്യുന്നു; പാണ്ഡവർ അദ്ദേഹത്തിന്റെ മന്ദിരങ്ങളിൽ രാത്രി കഴിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.159; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"यक्षयुद्धपर्व","titleEn":"Yakshayuddha Parva (Battle with the Yakshas)","verses":[{"text":"वैश्रवण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishravana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"युधिष्ठिर धृतिर्दाक्ष्यं देशकालौ पराक्रमः ।\nलोकतन्त्रविधानानामेष पञ्चविधो विधिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Yudhishthira, steadiness, skill, place, time and valour: this is the fivefold rule for managing the affairs of the world.\""}},{"n":2,"text":"धृतिमन्तश्च दक्षाश्च स्वे स्वे कर्मणि भारत ।\nपराक्रमविधानज्ञा नराः कृतयुगेऽभवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"In the Krita age, Bharata, men were steady and skilled in their own tasks and understood the ordering of valour.\""}},{"n":3,"text":"धृतिमान्देशकालज्ञः सर्वधर्मविधानवित् ।\nक्षत्रियः क्षत्रियश्रेष्ठ पृथिवीमनुशास्ति वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"A Kshatriya who is steady, who knows place and time and the rules of all dharma, best of Kshatriyas, rules the earth.\""}},{"n":4,"text":"य एवं वर्तते पार्थ पुरुषः सर्वकर्मसु ।\nस लोके लभते वीर यशः प्रेत्य च सद्गतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The man, Partha, who acts thus in all his undertakings gains fame in the world, hero, and a good end after death.\""}},{"n":5,"text":"देशकालान्तरप्रेप्सुः कृत्वा शक्रः पराक्रमम् ।\nसंप्राप्तस्त्रिदिवे राज्यं वृत्रहा वसुभिः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Knowing differences of place and time, Shakra, killer of Vritra, showed valour and gained kingship in heaven with the Vasus.\""}},{"n":6,"text":"पापात्मा पापबुद्धिर्यः पापमेवानुवर्तते ।\nकर्मणामविभागज्ञः प्रेत्य चेह च नश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The sinful-minded, evil-intentioned man who follows only sin, ignorant of the division of actions, is ruined here and hereafter.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"अकालज्ञः सुदुर्मेधाः कार्याणामविशेषवित् ।\nवृथाचारसमारम्भः प्रेत्य चेह च नश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"One who does not know the right time, is very dull, does not tell tasks apart and acts in vain is ruined here and hereafter.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"साहसे वर्तमानानां निकृतीनां दुरात्मनाम् ।\nसर्वसामर्थ्यलिप्सूनां पापो भवति निश्चयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"For those who act rashly, deceitful, wicked and wanting every power, the resolve is evil.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"अधर्मज्ञोऽवलिप्तश्च बालबुद्धिरमर्षणः ।\nनिर्भयो भीमसेनोऽयं तं शाधि पुरुषर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This Bhimasena is ignorant of dharma, arrogant, childish in mind, impatient and fearless. Rule him, bull among men.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"आर्ष्टिषेणस्य राजर्षेः प्राप्य भूयस्त्वमाश्रमम् ।\nतामिस्रं प्रथमं पक्षं वीतशोकभयो वस ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Come again to the hermitage of the royal sage Arshtishena and live there for the dark fortnight, free of grief and fear.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"अलकाः सह गन्धर्वैर्यक्षैश्च सह राक्षसैः ।\nमन्नियुक्ता मनुष्येन्द्र सर्वे च गिरिवासिनः ।\nरक्षन्तु त्वा महाबाहो सहितं द्विजसत्तमैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The Alakas with the Gandharvas, the Yakshas with the rakshasas, and all the mountain dwellers are placed under my orders, lord of men. Let them protect you, mighty-armed one, together with the best of brahmins.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"साहसेषु च संतिष्ठन्निह शैले वृकोदरः ।\nवार्यतां साध्वयं राजंस्त्वया धर्मभृतां वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let this Vrikodara, who persists in rash acts on this mountain, be rightly restrained by you, king, best of those who uphold dharma.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"इतः परं च राजेन्द्र द्रक्ष्यन्ति वनगोचराः ।\nउपस्थास्यन्ति च सदा रक्षिष्यन्ति च सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"From now on, king of kings, the forest dwellers will see you, will always wait on you and will guard you everywhere.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"तथैव चान्नपानानि स्वादूनि च बहूनि च ।\nउपस्थास्यन्ति वो गृह्य मत्प्रेष्याः पुरुषर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"My servants will also attend you with plenty of sweet food and drink, bull among men.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"यथा जिष्णुर्महेन्द्रस्य यथा वायोर्वृकोदरः ।\nधर्मस्य त्वं यथा तात योगोत्पन्नो निजः सुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"As Jishnu is to Mahendra, Vrikodara to the Wind, and you, dear one, to Dharma, his own son born through yoga,\""}},{"n":16,"text":"आत्मजावात्मसंपन्नौ यमौ चोभौ यथाश्विनोः ।\nरक्ष्यास्तद्वन्ममापीह यूयं सर्वे युधिष्ठिर ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"and as the twins, self-possessed and self-born, are to the Ashvins, so all of you are to be guarded by me here, Yudhishthira.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"अर्थतत्त्वविभागज्ञः सर्वधर्मविशेषवित् ।\nभीमसेनादवरजः फल्गुनः कुशली दिवि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Phalguna, who knows the divisions of true aims and the particulars of all dharma, younger than Bhimasena, is well in heaven.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"याः काश्चन मता लोकेष्वग्र्याः परमसंपदः ।\nजन्मप्रभृति ताः सर्वाः स्थितास्तात धनंजये ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Whatever supreme riches are reckoned foremost in the worlds, all of them have stood in Dhananjaya since birth.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"दमो दानं बलं बुद्धिर्ह्रीर्धृतिस्तेज उत्तमम् ।\nएतान्यपि महासत्त्वे स्थितान्यमिततेजसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Self-control, giving, strength, intelligence, modesty, steadiness and the best radiance all dwell in that mighty one of boundless splendour.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"न मोहात्कुरुते जिष्णुः कर्म पाण्डव गर्हितम् ।\nन पार्थस्य मृषोक्तानि कथयन्ति नरा नृषु ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Jishnu does no blameworthy deed through delusion, Pandava. Men do not tell of Partha's words as false among men.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"स देवपितृगन्धर्वैः कुरूणां कीर्तिवर्धनः ।\nमानितः कुरुतेऽस्त्राणि शक्रसद्मनि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Honoured by gods, ancestors and Gandharvas, he who increases the fame of the Kurus practises weapons in Shakra's abode, Bharata.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"योऽसौ सर्वान्महीपालान्धर्मेण वशमानयत् ।\nस शंतनुर्महातेजाः पितुस्तव पितामहः ।\nप्रीयते पार्थ पार्थेन दिवि गाण्डीवधन्वना ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The radiant Shantanu, your father's grandfather, who brought all kings under his sway by dharma, rejoices in heaven in Partha, the wielder of Gandiva.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"सम्यक्चासौ महावीर्यः कुलधुर्य इव स्थितः ।\nपितॄन्देवांस्तथा विप्रान्पूजयित्वा महायशाः ।\nसप्त मुख्यान्महामेधानाहरद्यमुनां प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He of great valour, standing like the yoke-bearer of the family, honoured ancestors, gods and brahmins, and, famed, performed the seven foremost great sacrifices at the Yamuna.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"अधिराजः स राजंस्त्वां शंतनुः प्रपितामहः ।\nस्वर्गजिच्छक्रलोकस्थः कुशलं परिपृच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"That overlord Shantanu, your great-grandfather, who won heaven and dwells in Shakra's world, asks after your welfare, king.\""}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":25,"text":"ततः शक्तिं गदां खड्गं धनुश्च भरतर्षभ ।\nप्राध्वं कृत्वा नमश्चक्रे कुबेराय वृकोदरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, bull of the Bharatas, Vrikodara laid down his spear, mace, sword and bow, and bowed to Kubera."}},{"n":26,"text":"ततोऽब्रवीद्धनाध्यक्षः शरण्यः शरणागतम् ।\nमानहा भव शत्रूणां सुहृदां नन्दिवर्धनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the lord of wealth, the refuge, said to him who had taken refuge: \"Be the destroyer of the pride of your foes and the increaser of your friends' joy.\""}},{"n":27,"text":"स्वेषु वेश्मसु रम्येषु वसतामित्रतापनाः ।\nकामानुपहरिष्यन्ति यक्षा वो भरतर्षभाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Tormentors of foes, bulls of the Bharatas, live in your own pleasant houses; the Yakshas will bring you what you wish.\""}},{"n":28,"text":"शीघ्रमेव गुडाकेशः कृतास्त्रः पुरुषर्षभः ।\nसाक्षान्मघवता सृष्टः संप्राप्स्यति धनंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Very soon Dhananjaya, lord of sleep, bull among men, having obtained the weapons and been sent by Maghavan himself, will come.\""}},{"n":29,"text":"एवमुत्तमकर्माणमनुशिष्य युधिष्ठिरम् ।\nअस्तं गिरिवरश्रेष्ठं प्रययौ गुह्यकाधिपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having thus instructed Yudhishthira of noble deeds, the lord of Guhyakas went to the Setting Mountain, best of mountains."}},{"n":30,"text":"तं परिस्तोमसंकीर्णैर्नानारत्नविभूषितैः ।\nयानैरनुययुर्यक्षा राक्षसाश्च सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thousands of Yakshas and rakshasas followed him in vehicles adorned with many jewels and crowded with coverings."}},{"n":31,"text":"पक्षिणामिव निर्घोषः कुबेरसदनं प्रति ।\nबभूव परमाश्वानामैरावतपथे यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sound of the best horses going along Airavata's path to Kubera's abode was like the cry of birds."}},{"n":32,"text":"ते जग्मुस्तूर्णमाकाशं धनाधिपतिवाजिनः ।\nप्रकर्षन्त इवाभ्राणि पिबन्त इव मारुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The horses of the lord of wealth went quickly through the sky, as if dragging the clouds and drinking the wind."}},{"n":33,"text":"ततस्तानि शरीराणि गतसत्त्वानि रक्षसाम् ।\nअपाकृष्यन्त शैलाग्राद्धनाधिपतिशासनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, at the lord of wealth's command, those lifeless bodies of the rakshasas were removed from the mountain top."}},{"n":34,"text":"तेषां हि शापकालोऽसौ कृतोऽगस्त्येन धीमता ।\nसमरे निहतास्तस्मात्सर्वे मणिमता सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"For that was the term of their curse, set by the wise Agastya, and so they were all killed in battle, along with Maniman."}},{"n":35,"text":"पाण्डवास्तु महात्मानस्तेषु वेश्मसु तां क्षपाम् ।\nसुखमूषुर्गतोद्वेगाः पूजिताः सर्वराक्षसैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great-souled Pandavas spent that night happily in those houses, free of anxiety, honoured by all the rakshasas."}}]}]}